  "sample": {
    "method": "Gumbel-max: choose argmax_j (logit_j / T + g_j) over the tokens that survived the filters, with g_j = -ln(-ln u_j) and u_j uniform in (0, 1). This picks token j with exactly its final renormalised probability.",
    "seed": 2,
    "seed_note": "Any seed is valid. This one was picked so the draw lands on a token other than the greedy choice, to show that sampling is not argmax; 'other_seeds' shows what seeds 0-9 pick with the same probabilities.",
    "position": 7,
    "rng": "u = (first 8 bytes of SHA-256('<seed>:<position>:<token_id>') as an unsigned integer, top 53 bits, plus 0.5) / 2^53, so 0 < u < 1. The draw depends only on (seed, position, token id), never on batch size or batch position. vLLM Model Runner V2 uses the same idea with a different hash (murmur3_hash32(seed, position, token_id)), so the numbers here are illustrative, not vLLM's.",
